  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is attached to a cord passing through a hole in a horizontal frictionless horizontal surface as shown in the figure. The block is originally revolving at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> from the hole, with an angular velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> . The cord is then pulled from below, shortening the radius of the circle in which the block revolves to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. Considering the block to be point mass, calculate the new angular velocity (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>rad</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>).<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0002_b30f72a15cf3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 106px; width: 230px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "By conservation of angular momentum<br />&nbsp;<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>M</mi><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.4</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.2</mo></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
